From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Realer Mason <stone-mason@dr.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 17:51:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] rust: extend miscdevice, kiocb and clk for the serial
 abstractions

Prepare the kernel crate for the out-of-tree Rust UART controller and
character device shipped by atk-dlrk3588-bsp:

- miscdevice: require an owning module (`MiscDevice::OWNER`) so an open
  file pins it, add a stream-open option, and add a `poll` callback with
  POLLIN/POLLOUT/POLLHUP/POLLERR constants;
- kiocb: expose the current file flags so write_iter can honour O_NONBLOCK
  changed with fcntl;
- clk: add `ExclusiveEnabledClk`, an enabled clock with an exclusive rate
  claim, which the controller holds on its baud clock while bound;
- bindings: pull in serial_core.h and tty_flip.h, export EPOLL* and UPF_*
  constants, and include the serial C helper file.

Update the in-tree misc device sample for the new OWNER constant.

[atk-dlrk3588-bsp] Glue from AnlangA/linux commit
28bc1e9c8cd1b933c95238811abf5b5700ff02b2. The new files of that commit
(rust/kernel/serial.rs, rust/helpers/serial.c) are provided by
linux/overlay/, the driver modules by linux/drivers/.
